    {
      "caption": "Wave speed equals frequency times wavelength",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s2",
      "narration": "For any wave, speed equals frequency times wavelength. Take this sound wave: it travels at 340 metres per second and vibrates 170 times per second. Its wavelength is 340 divided by 170 — 2 metres. Every number here ties together.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "title",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 34,
            "text": "The wave equation: v = f × λ",
            "x": 80,
            "y": 70
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 500,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#2471a3",
            "id": "formula",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 40,
            "tex": "v = f \\times \\lambda",
            "x": 80,
            "y": 170
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1500,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "given",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 24,
            "text": "Sound in air: v = 340 m/s,   f = 170 Hz",
            "x": 80,
            "y": 250
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "step1",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 24,
            "text": "Rearrange: λ = v ÷ f",
            "x": 80,
            "y": 320
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "work",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 36,
            "tex": "\\lambda = \\frac{340\\ \\text{m/s}}{170\\ \\text{Hz}} = 2\\ \\text{m}",
            "x": 80,
            "y": 400
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "check",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 24,
            "text": "Check: 170 Hz × 2 m = 340 m/s ✓  — it all agrees.",
            "x": 80,
            "y": 480
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "tip",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 22,
            "text": "Higher frequency at the same speed → shorter wavelength.",
            "x": 480,
            "y": 250
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 8600,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "v = f × λ. Change one, the others must balance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "We see lightning before we hear thunder",
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "Some people think sound travels faster than light. Watch a storm: the lightning flash arrives almost instantly, and the thunder rumbles in seconds later. Light races at 300 million metres per second; sound crawls at 340. Light is almost a million times faster — that is why flash comes first.",
